Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: follow OPP table changes in devfreq

mtk-svs init01 disables every GPU OPP except the fastest one that runs
at vboot, then checks that the GPU buck reads vboot. panfrost never
registered the devfreq OPP notifier, so the GPU stayed on its disabled
OPP and SVS failed for all banks:

  SVSB_GPU: buck voltage: 700000uV, expected vboot: 800000uV
  mtk-svs 1100bc00.svs: error -EPERM: svs start fail

Register it, so devfreq recomputes the available range and retargets
when OPPs are disabled, enabled or adjusted.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
@@ -212,6 +212,15 @@
 	}
 	pfdevfreq->devfreq = devfreq;
 
+	/*
+	 * Follow OPP table changes. mtk-svs disables every GPU OPP but the
+	 * one it calibrates at and then expects the buck at that OPP's
+	 * voltage; without the notifier the GPU stays on its disabled OPP.
+	 */
+	ret = devm_devfreq_register_opp_notifier(dev, devfreq);
+	if (ret)
+		DRM_DEV_INFO(dev, "Couldn't register OPP notifier: %d\n", ret);
+
 	cooling = devfreq_cooling_em_register(devfreq, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(cooling))
 		DRM_DEV_INFO(dev, "Failed to register cooling device\n");
